          <Option name="dualview/previewExpressions" type="List">
            <Option type="QString" value="coalesce(&#xd;&#xa;&#x9;lpad(&quot;sac_id&quot;, 5, 0),&#xd;&#xa;&#x9;lpad(&quot;fid&quot;, 5, 0)&#xd;&#xa;) || ' / ' || &quot;name&quot;&#xd;&#xa;"/>
          </Option>
          <Option name="embeddedWidgets/count" type="int" value="0"/>
          <Option name="userNotes" type="QString" value="&lt;!DOCTYPE HTML PUBLIC &quot;-//W3C//DTD HTML 4.0//EN&quot; &quot;http://www.w3.org/TR/REC-html40/strict.dtd&quot;>&#xa;&lt;html>&lt;head>&lt;meta name=&quot;qrichtext&quot; content=&quot;1&quot; />&lt;style type=&quot;text/css&quot;>&#xa;p, li { white-space: pre-wrap; }&#xa;&lt;/style>&lt;/head>&lt;body style=&quot; font-family:'MS Shell Dlg 2'; font-size:8.3pt; font-weight:400; font-style:normal;&quot;>&#xa;&lt;p style=&quot; margin-top:0px; margin-bottom:0px; margin-left:0px; margin-right:0px; -qt-block-indent:0; text-indent:0px;&quot;>&lt;span style=&quot; font-size:12pt;&quot;>The geometry of the route can be edited directly if exactly ZERO or ONE section is assigned.&lt;/span>&lt;/p>&#xa;&lt;p style=&quot;-qt-paragraph-type:empty; margin-top:0px; margin-bottom:0px; margin-left:0px; margin-right:0px; -qt-block-indent:0; text-indent:0px; font-size:12pt;&quot;>&lt;br />&lt;/p>&#xa;&lt;p style=&quot; margin-top:0px; margin-bottom:0px; margin-left:0px; margin-right:0px; -qt-block-indent:0; text-indent:0px;&quot;>&lt;span style=&quot; font-size:12pt;&quot;>If no section exists, a new one is created. If a section exists, the geometry is updated, resulting in a newly created assignment of the associated segments.&lt;/span>&lt;/p>&#xa;&lt;p style=&quot;-qt-paragraph-type:empty; margin-top:0px; margin-bottom:0px; margin-left:0px; margin-right:0px; -qt-block-indent:0; text-indent:0px; font-size:12pt;&quot;>&lt;br />&lt;/p>&#xa;&lt;p style=&quot; margin-top:0px; margin-bottom:0px; margin-left:0px; margin-right:0px; -qt-block-indent:0; text-indent:0px;&quot;>&lt;span style=&quot; font-size:12pt; font-weight:600;&quot;>Shorten a route&lt;/span>&lt;span style=&quot; font-size:12pt;&quot;>: Select the route and activate the function &amp;quot;Split Parts&amp;quot;. Split the route at the end of two segments. This creates a multipart linestring. Now activate the function &amp;quot;Delete Part&amp;quot;. Click on the part of the route which sholud be removed. This approach preserves the original attribute values of the route (and section).&lt;/span>&lt;/p>&#xa;&lt;p style=&quot;-qt-paragraph-type:empty; margin-top:0px; margin-bottom:0px; margin-left:0px; margin-right:0px; -qt-block-indent:0; text-indent:0px; font-size:12pt;&quot;>&lt;br />&lt;/p>&#xa;&lt;p style=&quot; margin-top:0px; margin-bottom:0px; margin-left:0px; margin-right:0px; -qt-block-indent:0; text-indent:0px;&quot;>&lt;span style=&quot; font-size:12pt; font-weight:600;&quot;>Extending a route&lt;/span>&lt;span style=&quot; font-size:12pt;&quot;>: Select the route you want to extend and activate the “Add segment” function. With tracing and object snapping activated: Click on the route before the end where you want to extend it. Digitize the extension of the route via the segments with tracing activated. Finish with the left mouse button.&lt;/span>&lt;/p>&lt;/body>&lt;/html>"/>
          <Option name="variableNames" type="invalid"/>
          <Option name="variableValues" type="invalid"/>
        </Option>
